    "turn_idx": 0,
    "turn_text": "And we are here with Senator Bill Cassidy. Thank you for joining us today, sir. We do appreciate it. My name is with you, David, publisher and editor of the news. Appreciate you all listening in. We're going to be talking with Dr. Bill Cassidy was actually a medical doctor. Lots of health care discussion today. But one of the first things we want to jump into is today at the state of the state address that Governor John Bell Edwards gave before the legislature started. We do have what is believed to be our first presumptive confirmed coronavirus in Louisiana. It was at a VA hospital in New Orleans. Senator Cassie, I want to jump in with you right now. You're actively working to contain the coronavirus through legislation. Tell us a little bit about that.",
